    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "I'm on tamsulosin, 0.4 milligrams, at night for the prostate.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:56",
      "end_timestamp": "04:01",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Putting it all together, it's hard to say. Symptoms that need an urgent cancer work-up is one possibility and a chronic infection another, and I'd rather not commit yet. We should do an urgent chest X-ray for cough and weight loss. I am referring you on an urgent pathway, which means an appointment within two weeks. The rapid diagnostic clinic would be the right next step, I'll refer you.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:02",
      "end_timestamp": "04:32",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]",
        "clinical_assessment[1]",
        "procedures_and_investigations[0]",
        "clinical_actions[0]",
        "clinical_actions[1]",
        "clinical_actions[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "the thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency. Book a review after the scans",
